+# Profile Page And Namespace Rename Design
+
+## Context
+
+The dashboard already has a compact profile modal backed by `/api/accounts/profile`.
+That modal supports email verification status, resending verification, Solana payout address updates, and password confirmation.
+The new work adds a full profile page that keeps those capabilities visible in a cleaner, more durable account settings surface.
+
+The selected rename behavior is a full account namespace rename.
+Changing a node name must move the public account identity and the owned repository namespace together.
+
+## Goals
+
+Add a professional profile page inside the existing dashboard shell.
+Keep the visual treatment quiet and consistent with the current dashboard.
+Expose the same account settings as the existing modal.
+Add node-name update only when the new name is valid, available, and the account email is verified.
+Add account disable as a soft-delete operation that preserves the database row.
+Preserve owned repositories and related repo-scoped data when the namespace changes.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+Do not add profile image uploads in this pass.
+Do not add password reset, email-change, key-rotation, or two-factor management flows.
+Do not redesign the dashboard navigation, repository list, network rail, or chat surfaces.
+Do not physically delete account rows or repository rows during account disable.
+
+## User Experience
+
+The sidebar profile menu will open a dashboard profile page instead of only opening the modal.
+The page will use the existing dark dashboard tokens, subdued borders, compact typography, and small controls.
+The first section will show a placeholder avatar, node name, email, email verification status, account status, and payout status.
+The avatar will use the same generated initial style as the sidebar for now.
+The account settings section will include email verification and Solana payout address controls equivalent to the current modal.
+The node-name section will include the current node name, a new node-name input, an availability status, and an update action.
+The danger zone will include account disable with explicit password confirmation and a confirmation phrase.
+
+The node-name action will stay disabled until all client-known gates pass.
+Those gates are a valid node-name shape, not equal to the current node name, available public lookup result, verified email in the current session, and a non-empty current password.
+The server will enforce the same gates because client-side checks are only user feedback.
+
+## Dashboard Structure
+
+The profile page will be a new `data-view="profile"` section in `public/dashboard.html`.
+The view will live inside the existing dashboard content area and will not use a separate landing page layout.
+The top nav can stay focused on repositories, network, docs, and blogs.
+The sidebar profile popover will include a `Profile settings` item that switches to the profile view.
+The existing modal can remain as a compact fallback if it is still referenced by tests or future UI.
+
+## Frontend Data Flow
+
+The dashboard will continue reading and writing `forkmesh.session` in local storage.
+Rendering profile data will update the sidebar, modal, and new profile page from the same session object.
+Saving payout details will continue posting to `/api/accounts/profile`.
+Resending email verification will continue posting to `/api/accounts/profile` with `resendVerification`.
+Checking node-name availability will use the existing public `GET /api/accounts/<nodeName>` lookup.
+Renaming the node will post to `/api/accounts/profile` with `newNodeName`.
+Disabling the account will post to `/api/accounts/profile` with `disableAccount`.
+
+Successful profile writes will refresh local session data from the server payload.
+A successful rename will also refresh repository data because owned repo owners and URLs may change.
+A successful disable will clear the session cookie and local storage, then send the user to the public homepage or login page.
+
+## Backend Contract
+
+`/api/accounts/profile` remains password-authenticated.
+The endpoint already accepts node name or email plus current password.
+The endpoint will add two optional actions: `newNodeName` and `disableAccount`.
+
+For `newNodeName`, the server will require an active account, a valid current password, a verified email, and a valid available target name.
+The target name is available only if no active or paid account already owns it.
+The server will reject a no-op rename to the current name.
+
+For `disableAccount`, the server will require an active account and a valid current password.
+The record will be kept in `accounts`, but its encrypted `status` will become `disabled`.
+Existing login already requires `status == "active"`, so disabled accounts will not authenticate.
+
+## Namespace Rename Semantics
+
+The account row is keyed by `name_bi`, which is the blind index of the node name.
+A rename will create or overwrite the target account row with the encrypted record updated to the new name.
+A rename will remove the old account row after the target row is safely written.
+The plaintext `accounts.name` value will move to the new node name.
+The `email_bi`, `ip_bi`, and `is_admin` values must be preserved.
+
+Repository rows are keyed by `key_bi`, which is the blind index of `<owner>/<repo>`.
+Owned repository rows must be rewritten from the old owner to the new owner.
+For each owned repository, the encrypted catalog record `owner` field will change to the new node name.
+Each owned repository row will move from the old `key_bi` to the new `key_bi`.
+Each moved repository row will update `owner_bi` to the new owner blind index.
+
+Account-scoped secondary rows must move where their key is the account blind index.
+Those rows include `account_presence`, `pending_verifications`, and `catalog_rate`.
+Login throttle rows can remain untouched because they expire and are keyed by the submitted identifier.
+
+Per-repo rows that use `repo_bi` must move from the old repo blind index to the new repo blind index.
+Those tables are `repo_shares`, `issue_inbox`, `pull_inbox`, `commit_inbox`, `discussion_inbox`, `host_presence`, `clone_rr`, and `repo_first_hosted`.
+Encrypted `repo_shares` payloads must also update their `owner` value so the collaborator UI lists the new namespace.
+
+Issue bounty rows must move from the old `bounty_bi` to the new `bounty_bi` because bounty keys are derived from `<owner>/<repo>#<number>`.
+Encrypted bounty payloads must also update their `owner` and `repo` values.
+
+Repo room history keys in `chat_history` must move when the `room_key` begins with `repo:<oldOwner>/<repo>:room:`.
+Project payout records in `funds_received` must update rows where `scope` is `project` and `key` is `<oldOwner>/<repo>`.
+
+Catalog cache must be cleared after a successful rename.
+Live Durable Object host sessions cannot be renamed in place, so clients will reconnect or republish under the new namespace.
+
+## Error Handling
+
+Invalid node names return `invalid_node_name`.
+Unavailable node names return `node_name_taken`.
+Unverified email returns `email_not_verified`.
+Bad password returns the same invalid credential style already used by profile updates.
+Conflicting target rows return a conflict status.
+Partial namespace moves should be avoided by validating all target keys before writes.
+If a write fails after validation, the endpoint should return an error and avoid clearing the old account row unless the target account row and repository moves have completed.
+
+## Security And Privacy
+
+The profile endpoint remains password-authenticated for all sensitive writes.
+Email verification is required for namespace rename to reduce account takeover impact.
+Public availability lookup must not expose private account metadata.
+Account disable is a soft-delete and must not erase audit-relevant encrypted account data.
+The UI should not imply that disabling removes database records.
+
+## Testing
+
+Add source-level backend contract tests for the new profile actions.
+The tests should assert that profile supports `newNodeName`, verifies email before rename, checks target availability, rewrites account identity, moves repository namespace keys, and soft-disables accounts.
+Add frontend contract tests for the profile page.
+The tests should assert the page exists, is reachable from the profile menu, contains profile avatar, email verification, payout address, node-name update, password confirmation, and account disable controls.
+Add client behavior checks for availability lookup, rename posting, disable posting, and session refresh or logout paths.
+
+Manual browser verification should cover desktop and mobile widths.
+The profile page should not overflow horizontally.
+The disabled states, error messages, confirmation flow, and loading states should remain legible and aligned.
+
+## Future Work
+
+The profile picture remains a generated placeholder in this implementation.
+Future upload support can reuse this page without changing the namespace rename contract.
